503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 277 0 R
/E (The proposed system, SafeGuard, is a comprehensive personal safety application designed to provide immediate assistance during emergency situations through an integrated and automated approach. The system enables users to trigger an SOS alert with a single action, which activates multiple safety mechanisms such as sending emergency messages to predefined contacts, sharing real-time location, and activating a siren for attention. Additional features like fake call simulation and hidden camera functionality enhance user safety by providing both preventive and evidence-collection capabilities. The application is built using React Native and TypeScript, ensuring cross-platform compatibility and a smooth user experience.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 277 0 R
/E (Furthermore, the system includes a dedicated admin panel that allows authorities to monitor user activities, manage emergency alerts, and handle complaints efficiently. By leveraging technologies such as Firebase for real-time data handling and secure authentication, the system ensures quick response and reliable performance. The centralized architecture improves coordination, reduces response time, and enhances overall safety management. This integrated approach makes SafeGuard a scalable, user-friendly, and effective solution for modern personal security challenges.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 277 0 R
/E (SafeGuard provides a set of core functionalities focused on ensuring quick and reliable emergency response. The application allows users to activate an SOS alert with a single tap, triggering actions such as sending emergency SMS messages, sharing live location, activating a siren, and initiating hidden camera recording for evidence collection. It also includes features like emergency contact management, fake call simulation for escape from unsafe situations, and quick access to emergency services. The system is designed to function efficiently even under stressful conditions, with a simple interface, countdown mechanism, and automated processes that minimize user effort.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 277 0 R
/E (The system involves two primary roles: the User and the Admin. The user interacts with the mobile application to manage contacts, trigger alerts, and access safety features. The admin, through the admin panel, monitors emergency requests, manages user data, handles complaints, and communicates with users when necessary. The admin also ensures proper system functioning by tracking incidents and updating their status. This role-based structure enables effective coordination, faster response times, and improved overall safety management.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
