793 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (The frontend of SafeGuard is designed to provide a simple, responsive, and user-friendly experience using React Native and TypeScript. It includes multiple interactive screens such as dashboard, emergency \(SOS\) interface, contacts management, safety features, complaint registration, and settings, along with an admin panel for monitoring and control. The interface is enhanced with real-time functionalities like live location tracking, instant alerts, and dynamic updates through Firebase integration, ensuring quick response without delays. With its clean design, dark mode support, large touch-friendly elements, and easy navigation, the frontend ensures smooth interaction and effective usability for both users and administrators, especially during critical situations.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
794 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (The backend of SafeGuard is responsible for handling data management, business logic, real-time communication, and integration between the mobile application and cloud services. It is primarily built using Firebase services, including Firebase Authentication and Firestore, providing a scalable and efficient backend infrastructure without the need for a traditional server setup.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
795 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (The backend manages core functionalities such as user authentication, emergency alert processing, real-time location updates, and storage of user data like contacts and complaints. It integrates APIs such as Google Maps for location services and SMS services for emergency communication. Additionally, the backend supports real-time updates for the admin panel, enabling monitoring of alerts, user activities, and complaint handling. With secure authentication, cloud data storage, and reliable performance, the backend ensures smooth operation, scalability, and responsiveness of the SafeGuard system.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
