/E (The system design of SafeGuard follows a modular and layered architecture to ensure scalability and efficient performance. It is a mobile-based application where the React Native frontend, Firebase backend, SQLite database, and external APIs like Google Maps)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
814 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 288 0 R
/E (The system architecture of SafeGuard is based on a three-tier model consisting of the presentation layer, application layer, and data layer. The presentation layer is the mobile frontend, developed using React Native and TypeScript, which allows users to interact with the system through screens such as dashboard, SOS interface, contacts, safety features, complaints, and settings. The application layer is powered by Firebase services, which handle request processing, business logic, user authentication, real-time data synchronization, and communication between users and the admin panel. The data layer includes SQLite for local storage of emergency contacts and Firebase Firestore for cloud-based storage of user data, complaints, and emergency records.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
815 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 288 0 R
/E (When a user performs an action such as triggering an SOS alert or registering a complaint, the request is sent from the frontend to the backend services, where it is processed and validated. The system then fetches or stores data in the database and may interact with external APIs such as Google Maps for location tracking and SMS services for sending alerts. The processed information is then updated in real time and reflected on both the user application and the admin panel. Additionally, security mechanisms such as authentication and permission handling ensure safe operation, while efficient data handling and real-time updates provide reliable and responsive system performance.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
816 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 288 0 R
/E (Input design in SafeGuard focuses on collecting user data in an efficient, accurate, and user-friendly manner to ensure quick interaction during both normal and emergency situations. Inputs are gathered through mobile-friendly forms, buttons, and interactive UI components such as SOS triggers, contact forms, and settings options, with proper validation to minimize errors and ensure reliability.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
