978 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (The SafeGuard System's ER diagram depicts a comprehensive relational database schema designed for emergency response, user safety, and efficient coordination among stakeholders.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
979 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 292 0 R
/T (Core Entities and Attributes)
/E (Core Entities and Attributes)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
980 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (Central to the model is the User entity with attributes like User ID \(primary key\), Phone Number, and Address, forming the backbone for all interactions. Connected entities include Emergency Contact \(User ID, Contact Phone\), Triggers, Location, SOS Alert \(SOS ID, Time Stamp, Status\), and Notification \(Date Time, Description\). Admin \(Admin ID, Role\) and Police Station \(Police ID, Station Name, Contact Number\) provide oversight and response capabilities.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
981 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (SAFEGUARD)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
982 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 293 0 R
/Pg 39 0 R
/A [3130 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
endobj
983 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
984 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Key Relationships)
/E (Key Relationships)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
985 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (The "Triggers" relationship links User to SOS Alert for real-time distress logging, while "Files" supports one-to-many attachments \(e.g., photos/videos\) with Date Time and Description. Location provides geospatial context, and Notification routes alerts to Police Stations, enabling rapid dispatch. Bidirectional "Manages" ties Admin to User for system control, with cardinalities like one-to-many from Police Station to Notification optimizing scalability.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
986 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Data Integrity and Features)
/E (Data Integrity and Features)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
987 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
988 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Scalability and Security)
/E (Scalability and Security)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
989 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (The schema scales for mass alerts via efficient indexing on Phone Number and Location, with room for extensions like Response Logs. Security emphasizes Admin role-based access, encryption for sensitive data \(e.g., Contact Phone\), and compliance through timestamped updates.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
990 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (This balanced design delivers reliability for a life-saving platform, prioritizing usability, response speed, and data protection..)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
