997 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 294 0 R
/T (10. AGILE METHODOLOGY )
/E (10. AGILE METHODOLOGY )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
998 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (After the initial study, it is found that the Agile model of software development is the most suitable method for developing the SafeGuard system. Agile methodology focuses on user satisfaction through continuous delivery of functional modules. Since the SafeGuard project consists of multiple independent features such as SOS alerts, contact management, complaint handling, and admin panel, these can be developed and delivered in phases, making Agile an ideal choice.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
999 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (Agile is a flexible and adaptive approach that allows continuous improvement through user feedback. In this project, the development is carried out in iterations, where each module is designed, implemented, and tested separately. This ensures faster development, easy error correction, and the ability to add new features like chat support and safety tools without affecting the existing system. Agile also promotes collaboration and efficient communication within the development process.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1000 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (Among the Agile methods, Scrum is selected for this project. Scrum is a lightweight framework used to manage complex software development. It focuses on delivering high-quality software in small time intervals called sprints. Each sprint produces a working module of the SafeGuard system, ensuring steady progress and better control over development.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1001 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (Scrum follows three main roles. The Product Owner represents the users and defines the system requirements such as safety features and emergency functionalities. The Scrum Master ensures that the development process follows Agile principles and removes any obstacles faced by the team. The Development Team is responsible for designing, coding, and testing the application modules such as SOS system, contacts, and admin panel.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
