2296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 317 0 R
/T (The rapid escalation of urban safety concerns has necessitated the development of sophisticated, technology-driven personal security solutions. This research introduces SafeGuard, a high-performance mobile application engineered using React Native and TypeScript to provide a multi-layered emergency response system. The application integrates real-time geolocation tracking, automated SMS alerting, and covert evidence collection to assist users in distress. Unlike traditional safety apps, SafeGuard employs a "security-through-deception" strategy, featuring a customizable fake call interface to deter potential threats non-confrontationally. The technical architecture leverages SQLite for robust local data persistence and Firebase for secure cloud-based authentication. A critical component of the system is the SOS trigger mechanism, which includes a five-second fail-safe countdown to prevent accidental activations. Furthermore, the application addresses the "golden hour" of emergency response by automating direct communication with both personal emergency contacts and official law enforcement agencies. Security is reinforced through a dedicated disarm password, ensuring that the emergency protocols cannot be easily bypassed by an aggressor. Experimental results indicate high reliability in coordinate precision and minimal latency in message delivery across various network conditions. This paper details the end-to-end development life cycle, from architectural design to real-world performance validation. Ultimately, SafeGuard represents a significant advancement in democratizing professional-grade security tools for the general public.)
/E (The rapid escalation of urban safety concerns has necessitated the development of sophisticated, technology-driven personal security solutions. This research introduces SafeGuard, a high-performance mobile application engineered using React Native and TypeScript to provide a multi-layered emergency response system. The application integrates real-time geolocation tracking, automated SMS alerting, and covert evidence collection to assist users in distress. Unlike traditional safety apps, SafeGuard employs a "security-through-deception" strategy, featuring a customizable fake call interface to deter potential threats non-confrontationally. The technical architecture leverages SQLite for robust local data persistence and Firebase for secure cloud-based authentication. A critical component of the system is the SOS trigger mechanism, which includes a five-second fail-safe countdown to prevent accidental activations. Furthermore, the application addresses the "golden hour" of emergency response by automating direct communication with both personal emergency contacts and official law enforcement agencies. Security is reinforced through a dedicated disarm password, ensuring that the emergency protocols cannot be easily bypassed by an aggressor. Experimental results indicate high reliability in coordinate precision and minimal latency in message delivery across various network conditions. This paper details the end-to-end development life cycle, from architectural design to real-world performance validation. Ultimately, SafeGuard represents a significant advancement in democratizing professional-grade security tools for the general public.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [7]
>>
