2307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 318 0 R
/T (A comprehensive review of existing personal safety applications reveals a landscape dominated by GPS-sharing tools and basic panic buttons. Early research in this domain focused primarily on "check-in" systems, where users would manually update their status to a central server. However, studies show that manual systems often fail during actual emergencies due to user panic or physical constraints. More recent iterations, such as "bSafe" or "Noonlight," have introduced features like voice-activated triggers and professional monitoring services. While effective, these often require high-cost subscriptions, making them inaccessible to low-income populations. Comparative analysis indicates that many apps lack a robust offline mode, rendering them useless in areas with poor cellular data connectivity.)
/E (A comprehensive review of existing personal safety applications reveals a landscape dominated by GPS-sharing tools and basic panic buttons. Early research in this domain focused primarily on "check-in" systems, where users would manually update their status to a central server. However, studies show that manual systems often fail during actual emergencies due to user panic or physical constraints. More recent iterations, such as "bSafe" or "Noonlight," have introduced features like voice-activated triggers and professional monitoring services. While effective, these often require high-cost subscriptions, making them inaccessible to low-income populations. Comparative analysis indicates that many apps lack a robust offline mode, rendering them useless in areas with poor cellular data connectivity.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
