2322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (Performance evaluations of SafeGuard indicate a significant improvement in response times compared to standard manual emergency procedures. In controlled testing environments, the average time from SOS trigger to the successful delivery of an SMS with location coordinates was recorded at 3.2 seconds on 4G networks. The location accuracy consistently stayed within a 5-to-10-meter radius, thanks to the utilization of fused location providers. Battery consumption during "Standby-Ready" mode was measured at less than 1.5% per hour, making it viable for all-day background operation.)
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
2323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (The hidden camera feature successfully captured identifiable images even when the main application UI was minimized, demonstrating the effectiveness of the detached view implementation. User testing sessions with a cohort of 50 participants revealed a 98% success rate in navigating to the SOS button under simulated stress.)
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
2324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (The "Fake Call" feature was rated as "highly realistic" by 92% of testers, who noted that the customization of caller ID was a critical deterrent factor. Stress testing the SQLite database with over 500 contact entries showed zero latency in retrieval times during the emergency loop. Furthermore, the siren's decibel output was verified to reach the maximum hardware limit of the device, effectively serving as an auditory deterrent. These results validate the technical architecture and the practical utility of the application in real-world scenarios.)
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
2325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 319 0 R
/T (CONCLUSION)
/E (CONCLUSION)
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
2326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (SafeGuard successfully demonstrates the potential of modern mobile frameworks to provide life-saving interventions through a well-engineered software ecosystem. By integrating real-time tracking, automated communication, and forensic tools, the application provides a comprehensive safety net for its users. The transition from a reactive tool to a proactive security partner is achieved through the inclusion of features like the "Fake Call" and the ERSS integration. Technically, the project proves that React Native, when combined with TypeScript and native modules, is capable of handling the high-performance demands of emergency software. The "local-first" data strategy ensures that the application remains functional even in the most challenging connectivity environments. Furthermore, the project's focus on user experience ensures that the interface remains accessible to individuals of all technical skill levels during a crisis. )
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
