4884 0 obj
<<
/Title (Personal safety remains a paramount concern in modern society, particularly for vulnerable demographics navigating high-risk environments. While the ubiquity of smartphones provides a platform for assistance, many existing solutions suffer from complex interfaces that are difficult to operate under extreme stress. The SafeGuard project was initiated to bridge the gap between complex security needs and the necessity for a streamlined, "one-tap" user experience. By utilizing a cross-platform framework like React Native, the application ensures that life-saving features are accessible to both Android and iOS users simultaneously.  The core philosophy of the application is proactive protection, combining immediate physical deterrents with digital evidence preservation. For instance, the integration of a hidden camera module allows for the discreet recording of incidents, which can later serve as vital legal evidence. Additionally, the inclusion of an Emergency Response Support System \(ERSS\) provides a direct link to national emergency numbers like 112. The application also addresses the psychological aspect of safety by providing users with tools like "Fake Call" to exit uncomfortable situations before they escalate. From a technical standpoint, the use of TypeScript ensures a type-safe codebase, reducing runtime errors in mission-critical scenarios. The system architecture is designed to be lightweight, ensuring that the app remains responsive even on lower-end hardware. This introduction sets the stage for a detailed exploration of how SafeGuard leverages modern mobile APIs to create a comprehensive safety net. As we progress, the paper will demonstrate how this integrated approach outperforms fragmented safety tools currently available in the market.)
/Dest [63 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4872 0 R
/Next 4885 0 R
>>
endobj
